# scripts/copy_lift.private.baseline — the ceiling for EXACT private copies of shared decisions.
# Held by `scripts/copy_lift.py --gate`. MEASURED at 99476a5, not chosen:
#   python3 scripts/copy_lift.py --private-copies --write-baseline
#
# An EXACT private copy is a function in an EMITTER whose normalized signature AND executable code
# equal a function in shared code, matched by SHAPE and not by the `FAMILIES` name list. Name
# matching is what `FAMILIES` already does, and that is why criterion 2 was unenforced: pasting
# `driver::streq` verbatim into `lower.al` under a fresh name left `--gate` at rc=0 with zero
# mentions of it (measured on this tree before the detector existed).
#
# WHY AN ADDITION RULE WITH A BASELINE: all 19 exist on main today, so refusing exact copies
# outright would turn the gate red before any new defect existed — a broken instrument, not evidence.
# AGENTS.md "Strict forms" is the same shape: refuse only a NEW occurrence, acknowledge what cannot
# move yet with `## copy-ok: #<issue> — <why>`. Held by NAME, so a removal is auditable and one
# copy swapped for another is not.
#
# CLASS, measured per name — the column that tells the next agent what is safe:
#   A  a PUB shared definition with IDENTICAL code exists -> delete the copy, repoint at it. Safe.
#   B  duplicated only across PRIVATE module copies, no pub home -> lift one to lower_ctx, then
#      delete the rest. Two steps, and the lift is the reviewed part.
#   C  a PUB version exists but its CODE DIFFERS -> NOT deletable by repointing; reconciling the
#      two implementations is a decision, and a naive "lift it" silently changes behaviour.
# Columns: class<TAB>name<TAB>emitter<TAB>home<TAB>call-sites-in-the-emitter
private=19
